"etf_notes_manual_lever_tran_info"=" Through daily position adjustment, the system makes profit increase and loss reduction of contract leverage positions in the bottom levels of Leveraged Tokens. This ensures that the user's leverage ratio is consistent with the agreed ratio.
Leveraged Tokens are divided into two kinds: timed position adjustment and no timed position adjustment, in which timed position adjustment refers that the platform will at the daily fixed time point execute position rebalancing management, used to ensure that Leveraged Tokens are in the agreed multiple leverage at the beginning of the day;
A no timed position adjustment refers to a temporary position adjustment when the actual leverage multiple of a Leveraged Token exceeds a certain level within a day, and the position is the agreed multiple leverage after the position adjustment";
